<figure class="cp-figure" data-history aria-labelledby="cp-history-title">
 <figcaption id="cp-history-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Find Mina’s orders, then find their status</figcaption>
 <div class="cp-options"><label>Secondary index <select data-cover><option value="no">Key columns only</option><option value="yes">STORING (status)</option></select></label></div>
 <div class="cp-scene">
  <div class="cp-lane" data-stage="0"><p class="cp-label">SQL gateway · requested result</p><p><code>customer_id = 1</code><br/><code>placed_at DESC, order_id DESC</code></p><p>Return order, time and status.</p></div>
  <div class="cp-arrow">↓ Search one customer’s interval</div>
  <div class="cp-history-indexes">
  <div class="cp-lane" data-stage="1"><p class="cp-label">Secondary index · customer, time ↓, order ↓</p><div class="cp-key"><code>1 / 20 Oct / 103</code><span data-status hidden>pending</span></div><div class="cp-key"><code>1 / 12 Oct / 101</code><span data-status hidden>paid</span></div><div class="cp-key cp-out"><code>2 / 14 Oct / 102</code><span>outside interval</span></div></div>
  <div class="cp-arrow cp-fetch-arrow" data-fetch-arrow>Primary fetches: keys 103 and 101</div>
  <div class="cp-lane" data-stage="2" data-primary><p class="cp-label">Primary index · order ID</p><div class="cp-key"><code>101 / customer 1</code><span>paid</span></div><div class="cp-key cp-out"><code>102 / customer 2</code><span>paid</span></div><div class="cp-key"><code>103 / customer 1</code><span>pending</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cp-arrow">↓ Return the requested order</div>
  <div class="cp-lane" data-stage="3"><p class="cp-label">Same answer</p><p><code>103 · 20 Oct · pending<br/>101 · 12 Oct · paid</code></p></div>
 </div>
 <p data-explanation data-live class="cp-explanation" aria-live="polite"></p>
 <div class="cp-controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 1 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step data-live></span><span data-hold class="cp-hold"><span></span></span></div>
 <p class="cp-caption">Mina’s history since 1 October, limited to ten; the small table has two qualifying orders. A logical key trace over the three shop orders, with an illustrative secondary index. Boxes show index contents, not physical ranges, requests or observed node placement. Exact timestamps are abbreviated to UTC dates.</p>
 <details><summary>Figure as text</summary><p>The customer-leading index puts Mina’s two orders together and newest first. Without status, their primary keys lead to two primary-index rows. Storing status supplies the answer at the secondary index. Both routes return 103, then 101; covering does not narrow the customer interval.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-history]').forEach(root=>{
  const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-cover]')!;
  const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw:(step:number)=>{
   const cover=select.value==='yes';
   root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-stage]').forEach(el=>el.classList.toggle('cp-active',Number(el.dataset.stage)===step));
   root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-status]').forEach(el=>el.hidden=!cover);
   root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-primary]')!.classList.toggle('cp-skipped',cover);
   root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fetch-arrow]')!.textContent=cover?'Status is already here · skip primary fetches':'Primary fetches: keys 103 and 101';
   const text=cover?['The SQL result needs order ID, time and status. The index has all three.','The same two entries are read in the same order. Their stored status values now travel with them.','No primary-index fetch is needed for this result. The primary data still exists and writes must maintain the secondary copy.','Return 103 pending, then 101 paid. The result and search interval stayed the same; the second access disappeared.']:['The result needs status as well as the ordering key. This secondary index does not hold status.','Read customer 1’s adjacent entries: 103 first, then 101. Order 102 belongs to another customer.','Use the two order IDs to fetch primary-index rows and obtain status. The engine can batch these fetches; two rows do not imply two RPCs.','Return 103 pending, then 101 paid. Finding two secondary entries was only the first part of this route.'];
   root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=text[step];
  }});select.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());
 });
</script>
